@startuml

state "Business lifecycle (jury wording)" as B {
  [*] --> AVAILABLE
  AVAILABLE --> RESERVED : guarded reserve commits
  RESERVED --> PAYMENT_PENDING : checkout begins before TTL
  RESERVED --> RELEASED : expiry / cancel
  PAYMENT_PENDING --> CONFIRMED : definitive payment success
  CONFIRMED --> SOLD : durable Inventory accounting\nin same local processing flow
  PAYMENT_PENDING --> RELEASED : definitive payment failure / cancellation
  SOLD --> [*]
  RELEASED --> [*]
}

state "Persisted Inventory reservation state" as R {
  [*] --> PR_RESERVED : reservation row inserted
  state "RESERVED" as PR_RESERVED
  state "PAYMENT_PENDING" as PR_PENDING
  state "SOLD" as PR_SOLD
  state "RELEASED" as PR_RELEASED
  PR_RESERVED --> PR_PENDING : checkout_id + outbox commit
  PR_RESERVED --> PR_RELEASED : release_reason EXPIRED or CANCELLED
  PR_PENDING --> PR_SOLD : guarded stock move + audit + outbox
  PR_PENDING --> PR_RELEASED : release_reason PAYMENT_FAILED or CANCELLED
  PR_SOLD --> [*]
  PR_RELEASED --> [*]
}

note bottom of B
AVAILABLE is an inventory quantity, not a Reservation row.
CONFIRMED is the business confirmation established by a definitive payment success.
SOLD is the authoritative durable stock/accounting state. The mapping has no external half-committed window.
PAYMENT_FAILED and TIMEOUT are outcomes/reasons; an UNKNOWN timeout retains PAYMENT_PENDING and is reconciled.
end note
@enduml
